1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:07,537
Today is September 21, 2026.

3
00:00:07,537 --> 00:00:15,846
Overnight, the S and P five hundred, Nasdaq, and Dow all firmed, with technology stocks anchoring the broader rebound.

4
00:00:15,846 --> 00:00:21,275
Treasury yields remain the single biggest macro constraint on equity valuations.

5
00:00:21,275 --> 00:00:25,209
The Fed dot plot still signals one more hike this year.

6
00:00:25,209 --> 00:00:29,951
But the market is pricing only a forty percent probability for October.

7
00:00:29,951 --> 00:00:35,172
That gap between official guidance and street pricing is where the real tension lives.

8
00:00:35,172 --> 00:00:37,954
The geopolitical tape is dense.

9
00:00:37,954 --> 00:00:43,628
Washington is slapping fifty percent tariffs on twenty billion Canadian dollars of goods.

10
00:00:43,628 --> 00:00:49,106
Ottawa has retaliated with tiered duties on twenty-seven billion in American products.

11
00:00:49,106 --> 00:00:54,118
Over eight thousand Canadian firms and a quarter million jobs are exposed.

12
00:00:54,118 --> 00:00:57,537
London is feeling the squeeze simultaneously.

13
00:00:57,537 --> 00:01:03,591
The Falklands question and Northern Ireland sovereignty are now open chips in US-UK talks.

14
00:01:03,591 --> 00:01:07,145
And Brussels just floated something unprecedented.

15
00:01:07,145 --> 00:01:11,826
Canada is being courted as the first quasi-member of the European Union.

16
00:01:11,826 --> 00:01:17,194
On the other side of the Atlantic, Beijing and Washington are in active dialogue.

17
00:01:17,194 --> 00:01:21,557
Deputy Premier He Lifeng led a delegation to the States this week.

18
00:01:21,557 --> 00:01:25,638
The market is pricing in hundreds of billions in tariff relief.

19
00:01:25,638 --> 00:01:29,988
The critical question is whether this is structural or merely tactical.

20
00:01:29,988 --> 00:01:34,363
Goldman Sachs has laid out its year-end all-assets rally case.

21
00:01:34,363 --> 00:01:36,532
The thesis is clean.

22
00:01:36,532 --> 00:01:39,890
Bond markets have overpriced the hiking cycle.

23
00:01:39,890 --> 00:01:45,956
Inflation cools, yields fall, and equities, bonds, and gold all benefit.

24
00:01:45,956 --> 00:01:48,616
But there is one hard prerequisite.

25
00:01:48,616 --> 00:01:50,699
Oil must come down.

26
00:01:50,699 --> 00:01:55,993
If Middle East escalation keeps crude elevated, the entire framework breaks.

27
00:01:55,993 --> 00:01:58,665
And that is the wildcard right now.

28
00:01:58,665 --> 00:02:02,023
The US and Iran are at a critical juncture.

29
00:02:02,023 --> 00:02:05,736
Riyadh sounded air raid sirens for the first time.

30
00:02:05,736 --> 00:02:09,412
Red Sea shipping corridors are under active threat.

31
00:02:09,412 --> 00:02:14,486
The Houthis have deployed AI voice synthesis to forge enemy retreat orders.

32
00:02:14,486 --> 00:02:19,143
This is a live, pricing-relevant threat to every asset class.

33
00:02:19,143 --> 00:02:26,103
This week also brings a six hundred billion short-term Treasury auction and a four hundred forty billion long-term issue.

34
00:02:26,103 --> 00:02:31,067
Weak demand pushes yields higher and compresses growth stock multiples.

35
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:33,824
Strong demand does the reverse.

36
00:02:33,824 --> 00:02:36,630
Japan is in a three-day holiday.

37
00:02:36,630 --> 00:02:39,510
The yen is flirting with one sixty.

38
00:02:39,510 --> 00:02:43,861
That is a five trillion dollar carry trade sitting on a hair trigger.

39
00:02:43,861 --> 00:02:49,302
In the tech complex, the software sector just printed numbers that reset the narrative.

40
00:02:49,302 --> 00:02:55,246
S and P software constituents beat earnings consensus by thirteen percent on average.

41
00:02:55,246 --> 00:02:59,375
Over eighty percent of names came in above revenue estimates.

42
00:02:59,375 --> 00:03:04,106
Goldman's cybersecurity basket is up sixty-five percent year to date.

43
00:03:04,106 --> 00:03:06,214
The market has pivoted.

44
00:03:06,214 --> 00:03:10,883
It is no longer pricing AI as a destroyer of legacy software.

45
00:03:10,883 --> 00:03:16,201
It is pricing AI as the engine that restructures and expands software margins.

46
00:03:16,201 --> 00:03:19,363
Trump has made his AI posture explicit.

47
00:03:19,363 --> 00:03:21,912
No restrictions on development.

48
00:03:21,912 --> 00:03:25,209
A dedicated AI czar will be appointed.

49
00:03:25,209 --> 00:03:30,246
OpenAI, Google, and Meta are greenlit to keep expanding capex.

50
00:03:30,246 --> 00:03:33,763
He called AI the next industrial revolution.

51
00:03:33,763 --> 00:03:38,162
He projected it could reach twenty-five percent of American GDP.

52
00:03:38,162 --> 00:03:41,214
The policy signal is unambiguous.

53
00:03:41,214 --> 00:03:45,197
Build faster, regulate lightly, scale now.

54
00:03:45,197 --> 00:03:48,934
But here is the divergence that matters for your portfolio.

55
00:03:48,934 --> 00:03:53,175
Hardware and semiconductors have already priced in that optimism.

56
00:03:53,175 --> 00:03:55,466
The rotation is visible.

57
00:03:55,466 --> 00:03:59,657
Money is migrating from chips toward software applications.

58
00:03:59,657 --> 00:04:05,037
If capex guidance disappoints even slightly, the hardware drawdown will be sharp.

59
00:04:05,037 --> 00:04:10,135
The software names have more runway because their earnings are just starting to inflect.

60
00:04:10,135 --> 00:04:15,454
The US-China talks this week are the swing factor for the entire tech complex.

61
00:04:15,454 --> 00:04:24,155
A meaningful tariff cut and easing of export controls would unlock valuation repair across export-oriented and China-revenue-exposed names.

62
00:04:24,155 --> 00:04:28,910
A hollow verbal handshake would trigger an immediate profit-taking cascade.

63
00:04:28,910 --> 00:04:32,390
The market needs substance, not soundbites.

64
00:04:32,390 --> 00:04:33,996
Nvidia.

65
00:04:33,996 --> 00:04:37,537
The story is no longer just data center demand.

66
00:04:37,537 --> 00:04:41,042
It is the entire AI infrastructure buildout.

67
00:04:41,042 --> 00:04:45,527
Every hyperscaler capex cycle flows through their GPUs.

68
00:04:45,527 --> 00:04:49,780
Institutional positioning is stretched, which means the bid is

69
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:51,937
real but fragile.

70
00:04:51,887 --> 00:04:56,079
The key technical level is the fifty-two week moving average.

71
00:04:56,079 --> 00:05:00,392
A close below that on volume signals institutional de-risking.

72
00:05:00,392 --> 00:05:04,069
Above it, the path of least resistance is higher.

73
00:05:04,069 --> 00:05:06,385
The risk is not demand.

74
00:05:06,385 --> 00:05:11,238
The risk is a single capex miss from any of the big four hyperscalers.

75
00:05:11,238 --> 00:05:14,902
That compresses the multiple before earnings catch up.

76
00:05:14,902 --> 00:05:18,738
Set your stop below the prior consolidation shelf.

77
00:05:18,738 --> 00:05:21,030
Do not chase a gap day.

78
00:05:21,030 --> 00:05:22,463
Tesla.

79
00:05:22,463 --> 00:05:24,927
The narrative has bifurcated.

80
00:05:24,927 --> 00:05:29,424
The automotive business is in a pricing war with Chinese OEMs.

81
00:05:29,424 --> 00:05:32,230
Margins are under structural pressure.

82
00:05:32,230 --> 00:05:37,463
But the autonomy and robotics optionality is what the street is actually underwriting.

83
00:05:37,463 --> 00:05:42,365
The robotaxi rollout timeline is the single variable that moves this stock.

84
00:05:42,365 --> 00:05:47,476
Watch quarterly deliveries against the one to two percent sequential growth threshold.

85
00:05:47,476 --> 00:05:50,846
Below that, the growth premium erodes.

86
00:05:50,846 --> 00:05:54,007
Above it, the re-rating accelerates.

87
00:05:54,007 --> 00:05:58,419
The fifty day moving average is the institutional line in the sand.

88
00:05:58,419 --> 00:06:02,451
A break below on above-average volume is your exit signal.

89
00:06:02,451 --> 00:06:08,566
The China revenue exposure makes this name directly sensitive to this week's US-China outcome.

90
00:06:08,566 --> 00:06:10,270
Microsoft.

91
00:06:10,270 --> 00:06:13,272
The software rotation beneficiary.

92
00:06:13,272 --> 00:06:18,530
Azure AI revenue is compounding at a rate that justifies the premium multiple.

93
00:06:18,530 --> 00:06:21,728
The beat-and-raise cadence has been consistent.

94
00:06:21,728 --> 00:06:26,299
But the valuation leaves no room for a single quarter of deceleration.

95
00:06:26,299 --> 00:06:30,110
The key level is the round number psychological support.

96
00:06:30,110 --> 00:06:33,713
Below that, algorithmic selling cascades.

97
00:06:33,713 --> 00:06:36,985
Above it, the momentum bid sustains.

98
00:06:36,985 --> 00:06:40,895
The AI agent product suite is the next catalyst.

99
00:06:40,895 --> 00:06:46,103
If developer adoption steepens in the next two quarters, the multiple expands.

100
00:06:46,103 --> 00:06:51,336
If it flattens, the stock trades as a mature software name at a growth premium.

101
00:06:51,336 --> 00:06:53,897
That is a dangerous combination.

102
00:06:53,897 --> 00:06:56,826
One final note before we close.

103
00:06:56,826 --> 00:07:00,833
The US-Canada-UK-Europe friction is not a trade story.

104
00:07:00,833 --> 00:07:03,333
It is a structural realignment.

105
00:07:03,333 --> 00:07:08,137
The post-war Western alliance is fragmenting along national interest lines.

106
00:07:08,137 --> 00:07:13,885
For your portfolio, supply chain diversification is no longer a long-term thesis.

107
00:07:13,885 --> 00:07:16,655
It is a quarterly earnings line item.

108
00:07:16,655 --> 00:07:22,647
Companies with single-region revenue concentration now carry a permanent geopolitical discount.

109
00:07:22,647 --> 00:07:26,655
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

110
00:07:26,655 --> 00:07:30,821
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
